Device memory: tell the guest memory service which host pages the GPU can reach.

EglantinePS5 packs cold 2 MiB slots of game memory (src/guest_memory_service.inc, EDEN_CRAM_PACK=1,
off by default). A GPU thread that reads a packed slot faults and unpacks it, and the runs where the
command reader ("GPU") did that were the ones with garbage draws. A weak hook,
eden_guest_gpu_cached(host, +1/-1), is now called for every page DeviceMemoryManager maps for the
GPU (Map/Unmap) and when a page's cached count goes from 0 to 1 or back, and the service never packs
a slot with such a page. Without the service (host tests) the hook is null and nothing changes.

